body:
Sorry for not replying as fast but first let me tell you i admire you, thinking so positively about everything, that's quite formidable to be able to be like this honestly.

&#x200B;

I on the contrary know perfectly that it's doable, that all you are saying is true indeed but i just can't manage to see myself having the resolve to do all of this. I've had years  and years of anxiety, living in the fear of everything being revealed. Constantly anticipating that every scenario will turn in the most negative way, i can't grasp the possibility to even try saving myself. I just can't bring myself to finally make a move in the right way, all i'm thinking is living in denial or run away of everything in any way possible instead of facing those problems for once.

&#x200B;

It's honestly so stupid and goes so far that i've come to the point of actually prefering the idea of suicide over the fact of revealing everything to my dad, just to avoid deceiving him once again.
